<description>&lt;p&gt;UN peacekeepers are accused of failing to protect civilians before the Abiemnom massacre that killed at least 213 people, and Amnesty International is calling for investigations into the authorities and UN. Clashes continue between government forces and opposition fighters in Akobo while governors in Jonglei and Aweil East urge peace ahead of elections scheduled for next month, which envoys warn could unravel fragile stability. A convoy ambush in South Sudan killed two people, including a journalist, and a CityLink Aviation plane crashed near Juba killing all 14 aboard. The humanitarian situation deepens with hunger, displacement and ongoing sexual violence, and 2 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxPeThJckdvVVVXeHlmS2Vpem5sZFVHRUF2QmdsT3dNRjN2Sy10SVZPeTM1cTJTYVFXd3YzTnprVXZaN0o3SkljdWJDQUZHOUMtY2NFMVhSWi03WFJwLUhwbFl4bEFTTldybkl4ZWg0QzVUM2NQRGtwa2hlTEdYcGRqbWpwaWJpWS1zME05MWo3TTlFN29tdExFcnVjY0tPalZHTzFfa0ZvdjVQejEyM3BTS0JpajlfQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxPVFoxQmpwenQtQ2xaV1hlMmh1RTNUZHFwWUxMZ3d0aUpQTUgxc2FVVmZDTlBOaUF5cjAwbVRDM2ExTXEzd0poVjluRHFLdTl2ZlNLQ1RUTlM3SmgtWTB6TlV0LUlhM3V4RV8weEhSZVA3M3I3SzRZOHNIMEdlQ0hNV3hrWHVPMGxNNG5V?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxPYW42YUZhSUNjMEtPY0l1UDh2N2o1cUdFMU1WRHBnQVpNdTJCNllHT3FvSlpzSEx6cTNKS3JCOWd1OGRqVHo3UjI4dVl0ZjZhaW1iMjJnRE5rYURod3RSVFB3dDNJU1d0RS1QeDd3ZERGLW8xSEF1WENMZnZMcE9qc0JrZzNRZUlibGg2N1ZINllfelN1anFmR1F3?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixwFBVV95cUxQX2luRkZSZ3VaTUZMd1hDMUJqaGNnQThh